{
  "slug": "si-subjuntivo-imperfecto",
  "number": 22,
  "part": 5,
  "level": "B2",
  "title": "If I were you…",
  "tagline": "The imperfect subjunctive and if-clauses: si tuviera, si hubiera sabido.",
  "goal": "Form the imperfect and pluperfect subjunctive and build real, unreal and past unreal if-clauses, plus como si and quisiera.",
  "minutes": 12,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "formas",
      "title": "The imperfect subjunctive",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Take the **ellos** form of the preterite, drop **-ron**, and add *-ra, -ras, -ra, -ramos, -ran*. Every irregular preterite carries over:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Preterite (ellos)", "Imperfect subjunctive"],
          "rows": [
            ["*hablaron*", "*habla{ra}, habla{ras}, habla{ra}, hablá{ramos}, habla{ran}*"],
            ["*tuvieron*", "*tuvie{ra}, tuvie{ras}…*"],
            ["*fueron* (ser, ir)", "*fue{ra}, fue{ras}…*"],
            ["*hicieron*", "*hicie{ra}…*"],
            ["*pudieron*", "*pudie{ra}…*"],
            ["*dijeron*", "*dije{ra}…*"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "note",
          "text": "You'll also see *-se* forms (*hablase, tuviese*), especially in Spain and in writing. They mean the same."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "si",
      "title": "Three kinds of if",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Type", "Structure", "Example"],
          "rows": [
            ["Real (possible)", "*si* + present → present / future", "*Si {tengo} tiempo, te {llamo}.*"],
            ["Unreal (now)", "*si* + imperfect subjunctive → conditional", "*Si {tuviera} tiempo, te {llamaría}.*"],
            ["Unreal past", "*si* + pluperfect subjunctive → conditional perfect", "*Si {hubiera sabido}, {habría venido}.*"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "warning",
          "text": "Never the conditional after *si*: «si tendría» is wrong. And never the present subjunctive after *si* either."
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "text": "pluperfect subjunctive = hubiera / hubieras / hubiera / hubiéramos / hubieran + participle"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "otros",
      "title": "Como si, quisiera and the past of wishes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Use", "Example", "English"],
          "rows": [
            ["*como si* + imp. subj.", "*Habla {como si} lo {supiera} todo.*", "as if he knew everything"],
            ["Polite request", "*{Quisiera} un café, por favor.*", "I'd like a coffee"],
            ["Wishes in the past", "*Quería que {vinieras}.*", "I wanted you to come"],
            ["Unlikely wishes", "*Ojalá {fuera} verano.*", "I wish it were summer"]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
